1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,066
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:02,829 --> 00:00:06,199
Lesson 3: Worlds Weather and Climate.

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,621
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:08,642 --> 00:00:10,003
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:10,603 --> 00:00:11,904
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:12,965 --> 00:00:15,847
Explain the difference between weather and climate.

7
00:00:16,688 --> 00:00:20,110
Identify and describe the factors affecting climate.

8
00:00:20,871 --> 00:00:23,433
Understand the different types of climate found

9
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:24,034
in the world.

10
00:00:24,874 --> 00:00:27,336
Recognize the climatic zones of the Earth.

11
00:00:28,197 --> 00:00:30,979
Explain how climate affects human life and

12
00:00:31,059 --> 00:00:31,779
the environment.

13
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,040
Start-Up.

14
00:00:33,861 --> 00:00:34,962
Look outside the window!

15
00:00:35,663 --> 00:00:36,283
Is it sunny,

16
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:38,125
cloudy, or rainy?

17
00:00:38,805 --> 00:00:40,767
Have you ever noticed how the weather

18
00:00:40,847 --> 00:00:42,108
changes throughout the day?

19
00:00:42,928 --> 00:00:44,770
Some places are always warm,

20
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:46,511
while others are cold.

21
00:00:47,272 --> 00:00:48,193
Why does this happen?

22
00:00:48,993 --> 00:00:49,794
In this chapter,

23
00:00:50,314 --> 00:00:52,836
we will explore the differences between weather

24
00:00:53,036 --> 00:00:55,859
and climate and understand the factors that

25
00:00:55,999 --> 00:00:56,699
influence them.

26
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:57,960
Weather.

27
00:00:58,901 --> 00:01:01,283
Weather is the condition of the atmosphere

28
00:01:01,544 --> 00:01:03,345
at a particular place and time.

29
00:01:04,246 --> 00:01:05,527
It includes temperature,

30
00:01:06,027 --> 00:01:08,570
wind, rainfall, humidity,

31
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:09,771
and cloud cover.

32
00:01:10,631 --> 00:01:12,713
Weather can change from hour to hour

33
00:01:13,074 --> 00:01:13,754
or day to day.

34
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:16,436
For example, one morning,

35
00:01:16,717 --> 00:01:18,879
it may be sunny and by afternoon

36
00:01:19,199 --> 00:01:19,839
it could rain.

37
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,101
Do You Know?

38
00:01:21,841 --> 00:01:23,924
The hottest place on Earth is the

39
00:01:24,024 --> 00:01:25,445
Lut Desert in Iran,

40
00:01:26,026 --> 00:01:28,609
where temperatures have been recorded as high

41
00:01:28,809 --> 00:01:34,875
as 159.3°F (70.7°C)!

42
00:01:35,536 --> 00:01:37,418
Imagine how hot it must be to

43
00:01:37,498 --> 00:01:38,619
have that much heat!

44
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:39,940
Climate.

45
00:01:40,861 --> 00:01:43,423
Climate is the average weather condition of

46
00:01:43,543 --> 00:01:45,345
a place over a long period,

47
00:01:46,045 --> 00:01:47,707
usually 30 years or more.

48
00:01:48,707 --> 00:01:50,349
It tells us whether a place is

49
00:01:50,429 --> 00:01:52,230
generally hot, cold,

50
00:01:52,831 --> 00:01:53,932
wet, or dry.

51
00:01:54,892 --> 00:01:57,414
For example, the climate of the Sahara

52
00:01:57,514 --> 00:01:59,176
Desert is hot and dry,

53
00:01:59,796 --> 00:02:01,978
while the climate of the Amazon Rainforest

54
00:02:02,318 --> 00:02:03,579
is warm and rainy.

55
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,164
Factors Affecting Climate.

56
00:02:07,246 --> 00:02:09,852
Several factors influence the climate of a

57
00:02:09,932 --> 00:02:10,312
place.

58
00:02:11,175 --> 00:02:13,199
Let us explore them one by one.

59
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:16,222
Distance from the Equator (Latitudes).

60
00:02:17,283 --> 00:02:20,245
The Earth is divided into imaginary lines

61
00:02:20,505 --> 00:02:21,646
called latitudes.

62
00:02:22,647 --> 00:02:26,029
Places near the equator receive direct sunlight

63
00:02:26,169 --> 00:02:26,990
throughout the year,

64
00:02:27,610 --> 00:02:28,491
making them hot.

65
00:02:29,572 --> 00:02:31,253
As we move towards the poles,

66
00:02:31,873 --> 00:02:33,094
sunlight spreads out,

67
00:02:33,675 --> 00:02:35,216
making these areas cooler.

68
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:38,418
This is why tropical regions are warm,

69
00:02:39,018 --> 00:02:40,800
while polar regions are cold.

70
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:41,761
Altitude.

71
00:02:43,002 --> 00:02:45,064
Altitude is the height of a place

72
00:02:45,304 --> 00:02:46,205
above sea level.

73
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:50,430
Higher altitudes have cooler temperatures because the

74
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:52,853
air is thinner and cannot hold much

75
00:02:52,953 --> 00:02:53,353
heat.

76
00:02:54,094 --> 00:02:57,337
For example, mountains are colder than plains

77
00:02:57,578 --> 00:02:58,799
at the same latitude.

78
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:02,802
Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and

79
00:03:02,882 --> 00:03:03,522
Land Breeze).

80
00:03:04,663 --> 00:03:07,324
Oceans and seas influence the climate of

81
00:03:07,464 --> 00:03:08,305
coastal areas.

82
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:11,727
Water heats up and cools down more

83
00:03:11,807 --> 00:03:12,847
slowly than land.

84
00:03:13,728 --> 00:03:14,428
During the day,

85
00:03:15,049 --> 00:03:16,990
land heats up faster than water,

86
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,351
causing a sea breeze to blow from

87
00:03:19,431 --> 00:03:20,572
the sea to the land.

88
00:03:21,472 --> 00:03:24,054
At night, the land cools down quickly,

89
00:03:24,594 --> 00:03:26,535
and a land breeze blows from land

90
00:03:26,835 --> 00:03:27,316
to the sea.

91
00:03:28,096 --> 00:03:30,638
This keeps coastal areas cooler in summer

92
00:03:31,038 --> 00:03:33,639
and warmer in winter compared to inland

93
00:03:33,719 --> 00:03:34,180
regions.

94
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:36,141
Direction of the Wind.

95
00:03:37,303 --> 00:03:40,026
Winds carry heat and moisture from one

96
00:03:40,106 --> 00:03:41,067
place to another.

97
00:03:41,848 --> 00:03:44,030
Winds coming from the sea bring rain,

98
00:03:44,771 --> 00:03:47,314
while winds from deserts bring dry weather.

99
00:03:48,054 --> 00:03:51,198
For example, the monsoon winds bring heavy

100
00:03:51,298 --> 00:03:52,419
rainfall to India.

101
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:53,841
Humidity.

102
00:03:54,842 --> 00:03:57,444
Humidity is the amount of water vapour

103
00:03:57,605 --> 00:03:58,145
in the air.

104
00:03:59,146 --> 00:04:02,550
Places with high humidity receive more rainfall,

105
00:04:03,191 --> 00:04:05,553
while dry areas have less humidity.

106
00:04:06,254 --> 00:04:09,898
For example, coastal areas have higher humidity

107
00:04:10,198 --> 00:04:10,939
than deserts.

108
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:12,981
Ocean Currents.

109
00:04:14,022 --> 00:04:16,724
Ocean currents are large movements of water

110
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:17,705
in the oceans.

111
00:04:18,746 --> 00:04:21,909
Warm ocean currents make coastal areas warmer,

112
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:25,052
while cold currents bring cool temperatures.

113
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:28,896
For example, the Gulf Stream warms Europe,

114
00:04:29,416 --> 00:04:32,299
while the cold Labrador Current cools Canada.

115
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:34,281
Let's Learn More!

116
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:38,407
Rainforests receive about 80 inches of rain

117
00:04:38,687 --> 00:04:41,190
each year and they are so important

118
00:04:41,651 --> 00:04:44,014
because they provide oxygen and food to

119
00:04:44,094 --> 00:04:44,494
the world.

120
00:04:45,235 --> 00:04:47,779
Without them, our planet would be very

121
00:04:47,859 --> 00:04:48,279
different!

122
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,063
Types of Climate.

123
00:04:51,025 --> 00:04:53,290
Different parts of the world have different

124
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:54,273
types of climate.

125
00:04:55,055 --> 00:04:56,598
Let's look at some major types.

126
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,503
Monsoon or Tropical Climate.

127
00:05:00,444 --> 00:05:01,686
Found in South Asia,

128
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:05,031
Southeast Asia, and some parts of Africa.

129
00:05:05,992 --> 00:05:08,516
It has hot summers and receives heavy

130
00:05:08,616 --> 00:05:10,679
rainfall during the monsoon season.

131
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,642
Equatorial Climate.

132
00:05:13,463 --> 00:05:14,845
Found near the equator,

133
00:05:15,346 --> 00:05:17,770
such as in the Amazon Rainforest and

134
00:05:17,870 --> 00:05:18,651
Congo Basin.

135
00:05:19,593 --> 00:05:21,656
It is hot and humid throughout the

136
00:05:21,736 --> 00:05:23,418
year with heavy rainfall.

137
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,402
Desert Climate.

138
00:05:26,364 --> 00:05:28,668
Found in places like the Sahara Desert

139
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:29,930
and the Thar Desert.

140
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,414
It has very little rainfall,

141
00:05:32,895 --> 00:05:34,879
hot days, and cold nights.

142
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:36,562
Tundra Climate.

143
00:05:37,463 --> 00:05:38,665
Found near the poles,

144
00:05:39,186 --> 00:05:41,450
such as in Greenland and Antarctica.

145
00:05:42,332 --> 00:05:44,957
It is extremely cold with little or

146
00:05:45,117 --> 00:05:45,979
no vegetation.

147
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,401
Do You Know?

148
00:05:48,202 --> 00:05:50,064
Antarctica is the driest,

149
00:05:50,485 --> 00:05:53,488
coldest, and windiest continent on Earth.

150
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,512
It hasn’t rained there in millions of

151
00:05:56,592 --> 00:05:59,776
years, but it’s still considered a desert

152
00:06:00,097 --> 00:06:01,939
because of the lack of precipitation.

153
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,404
Climatic Zones of the Earth.

154
00:06:05,487 --> 00:06:07,752
The Earth is divided into three main

155
00:06:07,853 --> 00:06:10,238
climatic zones based on latitude.

156
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,661
Torrid Zone.

157
00:06:12,463 --> 00:06:15,128
Located between the Tropic of Cancer and

158
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,430
the Tropic of Capricorn.

159
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:19,195
It is the hottest zone as it

160
00:06:19,275 --> 00:06:20,798
receives direct sunlight.

161
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,622
Temperate Zone.

162
00:06:23,444 --> 00:06:25,688
Found between the tropics and the polar

163
00:06:25,769 --> 00:06:26,210
circles.

164
00:06:27,071 --> 00:06:30,158
It has moderate temperatures with distinct seasons.

165
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:31,541
Do you know?

166
00:06:32,182 --> 00:06:34,165
There are different types of clouds that

167
00:06:34,245 --> 00:06:35,486
can tell you about the weather?

168
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:39,472
For example, cumulus clouds are fluffy and

169
00:06:39,572 --> 00:06:40,494
show fair weather,

170
00:06:40,974 --> 00:06:43,979
while nimbostratus clouds bring rain or snow.

171
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:45,702
Frigid Zone.

172
00:06:46,564 --> 00:06:48,008
Located near the poles.

173
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:51,457
It is the coldest zone with ice-covered

174
00:06:51,537 --> 00:06:51,919
lands.

175
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,081
Recall.

176
00:06:54,121 --> 00:06:56,964
Weather and climate are essential aspects of

177
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:57,805
our environment.

178
00:06:58,906 --> 00:07:01,228
Many factors, such as latitude,

179
00:07:01,708 --> 00:07:04,550
altitude, wind, and ocean currents,

180
00:07:04,991 --> 00:07:05,952
influence climate.

181
00:07:07,053 --> 00:07:10,135
Different regions experience different types of climates,

182
00:07:10,716 --> 00:07:12,177
affecting the way people live,

183
00:07:12,738 --> 00:07:14,719
the food they grow and the clothes

184
00:07:14,819 --> 00:07:15,219
they wear.

185
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,421
Let's Remember.

186
00:07:17,461 --> 00:07:20,283
Weather is the daily atmospheric condition of

187
00:07:20,383 --> 00:07:20,784
a place.

188
00:07:21,684 --> 00:07:24,086
Climate is the average weather over a

189
00:07:24,206 --> 00:07:24,926
long period.

190
00:07:25,787 --> 00:07:29,049
Latitude, altitude, distance from the sea,

191
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:31,571
and winds influence climate.

192
00:07:32,331 --> 00:07:34,453
The world has different types of climate,

193
00:07:34,893 --> 00:07:37,195
including tropical, desert,

194
00:07:37,555 --> 00:07:38,115
and tundra.

195
00:07:38,896 --> 00:07:40,977
The Earth has three climatic zones:

196
00:07:41,578 --> 00:07:43,959
torrid, temperate, and frigid.

197
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,400
Word Bank.

198
00:07:46,501 --> 00:07:46,901
Word.

199
00:07:47,682 --> 00:07:48,082
Meaning.

200
00:07:48,943 --> 00:07:49,543
Humidity.

201
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:52,325
The amount of water vapor in the

202
00:07:52,526 --> 00:07:52,926
air.

203
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:54,207
Altitude.

204
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:56,709
The height of a place above sea

205
00:07:56,789 --> 00:07:57,169
level.

206
00:07:58,010 --> 00:07:58,550
Equator.

207
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:02,153
An imaginary line dividing the Earth into

208
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:02,953
two halves.

209
00:08:03,934 --> 00:08:04,474
Monsoon.

210
00:08:05,195 --> 00:08:07,557
Seasonal winds that bring heavy rain.

211
00:08:08,497 --> 00:08:08,918
Tundra.

212
00:08:09,518 --> 00:08:12,080
A cold region with little vegetation.
